## 2. Core Differentiators\
\
### 2.1 Interactive 3D Human Body Visualizer\
\
> **The feature no other team will have.**\
\
Built with **React Three Fiber** (Three.js for React), the frontend renders an interactive 3D anatomical body model. When the AI detects organ-specific risk markers, the corresponding organ is dynamically highlighted in a severity color.\
\
- Liver enzymes elevated \uc0\u8594  liver glows amber/red\
- High creatinine \uc0\u8594  kidneys highlighted\
- Abnormal troponin \uc0\u8594  heart flagged as critical\
- Low hemoglobin \uc0\u8594  blood system visualization\
\
The user can rotate the model, click any highlighted organ to expand findings, and switch between skeletal and organ views. This turns a dry data table into an unforgettable demo moment.\
\
**Tech:** `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`, GLTF anatomical models, Three.js raycasting for organ click detection.\
\
### 2.2 Multi-Report Trend Intelligence\
\
Upload up to 5 historical reports. Vitalis extracts timestamped biomarker values and renders a time-series line chart with:\
\
- Per-biomarker trend lines (LDL, HbA1c, Hemoglobin, Creatinine, etc.)\
- A projected trendline showing where values are heading\
- A color-coded danger threshold line per WHO/ICMR reference ranges\
- A risk trajectory statement: *"Your LDL has risen 11% over 8 months. At this rate, it crosses the high-risk threshold by Q3 2026."*\
\
**Tech:** `Recharts` for charting, linear regression for projection, Claude API for trend narrative generation.\
\
### 2.3 AI Confidence Layer\
\
Every finding in the dashboard carries a per-finding confidence score derived from OCR quality and AI certainty. Low-confidence findings are flagged with a warning indicator, prompting the user to verify manually. This is architecturally honest and signals clinical maturity to judges.\
\
*Example: "LDL: 214 mg/dL \'97 High (AI Confidence: 94%) vs. "Platelet count: unclear \'97 OCR quality low on this value. Please verify manually. (Confidence: 41%)"*\
\
### 2.4 Patient \uc0\u8596  Doctor Mode Toggle\
\
A single header toggle switches the entire dashboard between two rendering modes using the same underlying JSON:\
\
- **Patient Mode:** Plain English, emoji severity indicators (`
\f2\b0 \uc0\u55357 \u57313 
\f0\b  Slightly Elevated`), lifestyle tips, relatable analogies\
- **Doctor Mode:** Clinical terminology, ICD-10 diagnostic hints, standard reference ranges, abbreviated clinical language\
\
### 2.5 Vernacular Audio Readout\
\
A text-to-speech engine reads the simplified health summary aloud in the user's selected regional language. Supports Hindi, Marathi, Tamil, and Bengali using the Web Speech API with language-specific `SpeechSynthesisUtterance` voices, with fallback to Google Cloud Text-to-Speech for unsupported voices.\
\
This makes Vitalis genuinely accessible to rural and semi-literate patients \'97 a strong social impact signal for Indian judges.\
\
### 2.6 Location Intelligence: Specialist Finder\
\
After analysis, Vitalis maps the nearest top-rated specialists relevant to the specific findings using spatial clustering. A patient with high creatinine sees nephrologists. A patient with elevated liver enzymes sees hepatologists. Powered by **Google Maps API** with Places API for specialist discovery.\
\
### 2.7 Printable Action Plan\
\
One-click PDF export of a personalized 7-day plan: specific foods, foods to avoid, recommended specialist type, and one primary lifestyle change. Generated by Claude, formatted with `window.print()` + a dedicated print CSS stylesheet. A judge who can physically hold this output remembers the demo.\
\
